Fuzz targets for the revisionstore on-disk read paths.

The stores under eden/scm/lib/indexedlog/fuzz cover the container format. These
cover the revisionstore layer above it: the entry decoders of the three stores
that keep data in an indexedlog, reached through their store wrappers.

  entry_decode          indexedlogdatastore: Entry::from_bytes,
                        InternalMetadata::read and Entry::calculate_content,
                        reached via get_raw_entry and to_keys
  store_open_get        IndexedLogHgIdDataStore::new on a corrupted rotated
                        store, then get/get_missing/to_keys - the Log::lookup
                        frame the EdenFS crash reports name
  aux_entry_decode      indexedlogauxstore: deserialize, reached via
                        AuxStore::get - the version byte, the VLQ total_size
                        and the file header metadata size
  lfs_blob_decode       lfs: LfsIndexedLogBlobsStore::get, reached via
                        LfsStore::get_blob - the mincode chunk decode and the
                        range/data stitching loop

indexedlog checksums every entry it stores, so an entry patched on disk is
rejected below revisionstore and the decoder never runs. Every target except
store_open_get therefore patches a valid serialized entry and appends it
through a store's write path, which recomputes the checksum over the patched
bytes. store_open_get patches the container files instead. All of them encode
the input as a sequence of 8-byte patch records; see
eden/scm/lib/fuzzutil/src/corrupt.rs.

Panics, aborts and sanitizer reports are findings. Errors returned for corrupt
data are the expected behavior and are ignored by the harnesses.

Run with buck2. Every length and offset these decoders read is a VLQ, so pass
the shared boundary dictionary:

    buck2 run @fbcode//mode/opt-asan -c rust.fuzzing=true \
        fbcode//eden/scm/lib/revisionstore/fuzz:entry_decode -- \
        -dict=fbcode/eden/scm/lib/fuzzutil/vlq.dict -runs=100000 /path/to/corpus

store_open_get calls `fuzzutil::configure_indexedlog_for_fuzzing` before
writing its seed, which makes indexedlog use a fixed epoch and skip the
index-lag timestamp, so the snapshot is byte-identical across processes and
offset-based patches replay deterministically.

mode/opt-asan matters: tools/build_defs/lib/rust/rust_common.bzl gives DEFAULT
and asan-ubsan-dev builds an empty sancov flag list, so those binaries build and
run but collect no coverage. Confirm instrumentation before trusting a run:

    readelf -S <binary> | grep -E "__sancov_cntrs|__sancov_pcs"

Steps to run the fuzz tests with the OSS toolchain:

1. Install rustup.
2. `rustup install nightly` to install the nightly toolchain.
3. From `eden/scm`, run `rustup override set nightly && make local` to use the
   nightly toolchain.
4. From `revisionstore` (parent directory of `fuzz`), run
   `cargo fuzz run $TEST_NAME`.

See also https://rust-fuzz.github.io/book/cargo-fuzz.html.
